                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "30764366",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198032089697",
                            "num_reviews": 30,
                            "playtime_forever": 10,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 10,
                            "last_played": 1490576790
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Gosh, I wish I was ambidextrous, the things I could do. My work, my fun time, my sex life, all of it would be great. What’s that I hear you say?! No! Ambidextrous is not Dexter driving an ambulance in a killing spree! It is when you equally use your left and right hands. Where the hell was your devious mind?\n\nLike me, if you want to sharpen your Homer-ish mind (the yellow guy, not the greek philosopher) and your Ninja-less reflexes, then lets take a look at Twixel. \n\nStory\nThere is none, make it up as you go. Live with it.\n\nGame Play\nGame play is so simple yet fun. You control two boxes that must traverse a downwards scrolling maze. Sounds so simple it should be a breeze….. guess what princess, it’s not. \n\nYou control the left box with your left hand on the A & D keys and the right box with the right hand on left and right arrow keys. You slide the boxes left and right simultaneously, avoiding obstacles as they come down. You can hit the sides walls to you hearts content but hit an obstacle and you might as well throw both your hands in the air and scream “Rimmer is a Smeg-head!”\n\nYou must navigate these mazes as long as you can because if you can last for 60 seconds or more, you get to unlock more fiendishly hard levels. If not, then take heed of these words of wisdom from Master Yoda “Do or Do not, there is no Frys….. with Burger of mine, Yes!”\n\nThe are 6 levels (or styles) to choose. Pixel, Vector and Polygon with Hyper Pixel/Vector/Polygon being unlock when you last past 60 seconds, and if you last 60 seconds in all of those, you unlock the Twixel (if you can, then your an ambidextrous Super-Sayan or a bloody Vulcan!)\n\nEverything Else\nThere is no mouse support (it would be nice) so navigation through the game and option is via left and right arrow keys and space bar. You have the option of 2D and 3D graphic and music volume. Music is annoying so turn it off and go with some Def Leppard on this one. Graphics is just simple box style so nothing to get excited over, but it is clean with no unwanted pixeling.\n\nSo if your training to throw daggers with both hands, or double wield MG42’s then Twixel by Caesoose Studios is your goto training app, if not, then you better find something else to do with your two hands. \n\n\nOriginal review posted here  https://muut.com/cassus#!/action  For all your Indie Gaming discussion",
